.TH fleetring-control 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-control \- Adds, lists, and removes control nodes, and sets the voters
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring control\fR [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds, lists, and removes control nodes, and sets the voters
.PP
The control group is the control nodes that replicate the control log (ADR\-0040). Grow it from one control node to three with two `control add` and one `control set\-voters`; take a node out with `control set\-voters` without it, then `control remove`.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
When to colour log lines and the picker: auto, always, or never

`auto`, the default, colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
fleetring\-control\-add(1)
Adds a control node to the control group as a learner
.TP
fleetring\-control\-set\-voters(1)
Makes exactly these control nodes the voters
.TP
fleetring\-control\-remove(1)
Removes a learner from the control group
.TP
fleetring\-control\-list(1)
Lists the control group\*(Aqs voters and learners, and which one leads
